arn  the importance of situational awareness  and being able to have that right level  of insanity while being able to process  what's going on and therefore if you  can't process what's going on you're not  gonna have much fun ultimately so we  pared it down to a point and we got to a  point we thought this is enough  craziness to feel exciting and dynamic  vibrant at the same time it's not so  much that I can't quite grasp what's  going on or if I'm you know I'm getting  hit from too many sides it was another  unique element of Titan force  development is how respawn have  discarded the traditional split between  single-player campaign and multiplayer  in title for the campaign is played  through multiplayer alongside others  levels are joined together by story  trappings which appear in various places  such as the start of a mission we asked  Vince Zampella if this was a decision to  try and do something new or a reality of  working with a smaller team I would say  it's something that when we started  making the game you look at you know the  amount of resources that you have and  your goals and our goal was definitely  multiplayer we want to take multiplayer  to the next level so how do we do that  okay you look at the amount of resources  that you put into a single-player game  that people breeze through in you know  five six hours or not at all and then  you know the multiplayer kind of gets  you know what's left over we didn't want  that so we said we're going to take that  and part of the goal is if you're gonna  make multiplayer better what do you do  you want to make the world more  believable more engaging so you take  those great single-player elements that  you know pull them over put them into  multiplayer so now this worlds more  alive there's things going on around you  there is you know there's grunts running  around there's no it's just a more  believable world  and all that content gets seen by so  many more people and it gets played for  hundreds of hours and you know so for us  it was just kind of a natural fit based  on our desires and the amount of work  that we had to do as we approach launch  there seems to be a skip in the step of  the people that make up respawn after  four years of working together they're  just about ready to release their  creation on to the world and it seems  they're looking forward to it working on  titanfall and like thinking about it  launching and just just a very short  time away it's like giving birth in  public you know it's a not that I will  ever give birth give birth in my life  but it's it's it's this crazy thing we  don't want to let anybody down so we've  been incredibly hard on ourselves I just  hope that it's a game that everybody  likes and wants to play and you know  tries it out I mean I think we're all  super excited for people to play this  thing I know when we were doing the  Alpha everybody on the team was spending  like their entire weekends playing with  everybody else and just watching them  and exchanging stories and you know we  were had we had to be quiet we didn't  want people to know we were devs but we  would listen to the feedback that people  were going and they would just be  talking about what happened holy [ __ ] I  can't believe I acted I lie not tied he  ejected shot us both up we went into an  aerial fight and it's just like you were  listening a guy yeah you're playing  titanfall  I would say that it's a really really  really fun game with a lot of depth and  a lot of variety as well depth and  breadth it's very it's probably the most  cinematic wild multiplayer experience we  have and I guess what I'm really excited  buzz fact that people are gonna make  some crazy videos you know it's been a  long kind of road to be where we are to  rally the team together get through all  the adversity that we face and get to a  point where we're releasing something  that you know we're proud of and is  being so just it being accepted by the  fans and by everyone you know just so  well it means a lot it's it feels good  that was the folks at Respawn  Entertainment giving us an insight into  the creative process behind titanfall  but we're not quite done with them yet  make sure you check back on gamespot  comm or this week for continuing  coverage of the game including a look  into the relationship between pilots and  Titans and a one-on-one with the founder  of respawn mr. Vince and Pella see you  then  [Music]
 

